WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.176 --> 00:00:14.610
 Hi, everyone.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.270
I'm Justin K. Thompson,
and I am the production

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.690
designer for Spider-Man:
Into the Spider-Verse.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:22.730
When we were working
on the animated film,

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.800
the most exciting
part of the process

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.720
was bringing Miles
Morales to life

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.330
on the big screen for the
first time in a way that

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.490
had never been seen before.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.440
We knew how special
the character was,

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.990
and that we wanted to give
him his own unique style

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.160
of animation.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.410
And it's been amazing
to see the way audiences

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.540
have responded to the movie.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.750
And now, it's exciting to
see that Insomnia Games

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.390
and PlayStation in
collaboration with Marvel Games,

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.400
created its own take
on the character

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.520
in Marvel's Spider-Man:
Miles Morales,

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.400
coming out for PS5 and PS4.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.670
The way Insomniac faithfully
brought the iconic suit

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.790
designed for Spider-Man: Into
the Spider-Verse into the game

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.430
is visually stunning
and remarkable.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.730
We were able to advise on some
of the unique design elements

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:11.300
that made the film so distinct,
like how we often animated

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.630
the characters on twos, and we
made recommendations for how

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.700
best to integrate
the pop up words

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.500
and the little burst
cards on screen

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.206
into the action sequences.

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:24.440
 Hey, The Underground's
messing with a billboard.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:25.617
Just pinged it.

00:01:42.018 --> 00:01:44.160
 The Underground must
be nearby if they're

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.861
hijacking that billboard.

00:01:51.753 --> 00:01:54.077
Got to lock on to the
signal so I can find

00:01:54.077 --> 00:01:55.110
where the Underground's hiding.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.302
Locking on.

00:02:04.302 --> 00:02:05.721
All right.

00:02:05.721 --> 00:02:08.086
Now to track them down.

00:02:08.086 --> 00:02:11.920
The Underground's trying to get
the press to notice them more.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.080
Maybe they should launch an ad.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.510
The Underground, as advertised.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.200
UNDERGROUND: Do you
think anyone's--

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.908
 How's building that
Underground brand going?

00:02:50.908 --> 00:02:53.398
UNDERGROUND: I'll show
you what we can do!

00:02:53.398 --> 00:02:54.892
UNDERGROUND: You
can't even see him!

00:02:54.892 --> 00:02:56.884
UNDERGROUND: Take him down!

00:02:56.884 --> 00:02:59.374
UNDERGROUND: Can't wait
to rip that mask off!

00:03:06.844 --> 00:03:08.338
You won't stop us!

00:03:13.879 --> 00:03:14.812
This your warning-- go home!

00:03:19.294 --> 00:03:20.290
Take your best shot!

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:25.270
It won't--

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.210
 There's gotta be a
transmitter around here.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.800
Friendly neighborhood
Spider-Man-- one.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:54.120
Underground advertising
campaign-- zero.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.805
Something's weakening emergency
responder communications.

00:04:35.805 --> 00:04:36.750
Should check it out.

00:05:05.402 --> 00:05:07.830
 Spider-Man, thank god.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.780
Something's weakening
our emergency comms.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.252
We can't get through
to the fire department.

00:05:12.252 --> 00:05:14.075
 Is anyone still inside?

00:05:14.075 --> 00:05:16.070
 No, we got everyone out.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:18.690
But this fire's going to
jump if we don't get help.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:19.490
Hear that?

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:21.090
Just noise now.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:23.160
 I think I can find the source.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:23.960
Don't worry.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:26.351
I'm going to get
your comms back up.

00:05:26.351 --> 00:05:28.510
The sooner I get to
the source, the sooner

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:29.590
the fire trucks get here.

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:31.770
My webs can't handle
a fire this big.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.020
Whatever is weakening
the signal is just ahead.

00:05:54.065 --> 00:05:57.610
 Fire's burning real good,
and all I'm hearing is static.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.290
Guess powering down
the tower worked.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.870
 Insurance only pays out if
the whole building goes down.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:04.505
So make sure the
static stays till then.

00:06:04.505 --> 00:06:07.570
 They're weakening comms
for an insurance scam?

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:08.440
Got to stop them.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:11.510
CRIMINAL: Hey, you sure you
know what you're doing there?

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:14.890
CRIMINAL: Yeah, I watched
one of those video tutorials.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:17.533
Seriously, there's one for
everything on the internet.

00:06:17.533 --> 00:06:19.583
CRIMINAL: Oh, don't show up.

00:06:27.471 --> 00:06:29.920
CRIMINAL: I hate
New York winters.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.260
I haven't felt my
toes in a week.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.814
CRIMINAL: Payday is going
to be sweet on this one.

00:06:34.814 --> 00:06:35.910
CRIMINAL: You know it.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.440
Just gotta wait a
little while longer.

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:38.990
 Sorry guys.

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:41.636
You really should've gone
for the Spider-Man insurance.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:02.020
Comms are weak because
there's no power.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.178
I need to charge
up that generator.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.100
Hey Mr. EMT.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.780
Dudes are trying to
burn down that building

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.280
for an insurance scam.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.960
That's why they're
messing with your comms.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.100
EMT: Are you serious?

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.945
They're putting
people in danger.

00:07:17.945 --> 00:07:19.130
 Yeah.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.030
How's the fire looking?

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:22.530
EMT: It's getting real close to
jumping the building next door.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:24.495
And I still can't reach
the fire department.

00:07:24.495 --> 00:07:26.550
 Signal should be clear soon.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.350
Hang tight.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:28.150
I'll update you.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:49.130
Getting close.

00:07:55.094 --> 00:07:56.780
CRIMINAL: Hang on.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.890
The signal's stronger now.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:07:59.840
What did you do?

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:02.330
CRIMINAL: Why are you always
assuming things are my fault?

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:03.320
Huh?

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:04.175
What's that about?

00:08:04.175 --> 00:08:05.487
 Can't wait.

00:08:05.487 --> 00:08:06.920
I've got to get those
comms back to normal.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.500
CRIMINAL: Kind of feeling a
little bad for the neighbors.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.760
What if the fire spreads?

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.700
CRIMINAL: You must be new here.

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:14.780
CRIMINAL: Spider-Man!

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:18.044
Whoever takes him
out gets a bonus!

00:08:18.044 --> 00:08:19.930
CRIMINAL: He just
freakin' vanished!

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:23.220
He's over here!

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:28.408
CRIMINAL: Stay out of
my business freak show!

00:08:28.408 --> 00:08:29.899
CRIMINAL: He's mine!

00:08:34.896 --> 00:08:35.863
CRIMINAL: Any luck with this?

00:08:38.845 --> 00:08:41.827
CRIMINAL: This ain't
gonna end well for you.

00:08:55.743 --> 00:08:58.080
 Now to get the comms
back to full power.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:01.560
There.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.260
Think that worked.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:06.980
I should check on the fire and
make sure comms are back up.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:08.420
Hey, how's the signal now?

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:10.760
EMT: Everything is coming
through loud and clear.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.340
Got through to dispatch too.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:13.480
Fire trucks are pulling up now.

00:10:03.617 --> 00:10:04.750
 Fire department
got the building

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.570
extinguished just in time.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:08.760
I'm definitely giving
your app five stars.

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:10.110
 Glad I could help.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:11.700
Spread the word, too.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.530
The more people use the app,
the safer we'll make New York.

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:16.840
 I'm going to make sure
everybody knows about it.

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.206
Thanks again, Spider-Man.

00:10:29.384 --> 00:10:31.270
 Mom was right.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:32.195
Neighborhood's gorgeous.

00:11:05.618 --> 00:11:09.170
 I myself am a huge
fan of comic books.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:11.620
So I'm excited that
fans like me will get

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:13.570
the opportunity to
play a game with Miles

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.760
Morales in the lead role.

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:18.370
Thank you to Insomniac,
our friends at PlayStation,

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:22.250
and Marvel Games for inviting
me to be a part of this video.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:23.950
We can't wait to see
it all come together.

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:30.300
ANNOUNCER: PlayStation.

